title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Duplicate or archive a workflow
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: Duplicate makes a separate draft with the same steps, which keeps a link to the original. Archive retires a workflow: new cases stop using it, cases that follow it keep their version, and its history stays. An archived workflow can be read and duplicated, not edited or published.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click 'More' in the bar"
screen mn "'Duplicate' - 'A new draft with the same steps'\n'Version history' - 'Earlier versions and who saved them'\n'Archive' - 'Retire it. It stops being used for new cases'"
click c1 "Click 'Duplicate'"
decision d1 "Unsaved changes?"
overlay o0 "'Leave without saving?'"
store st1 "A copy is made: 'Name (copy)', version 1, Draft\nIt keeps a link to the workflow it came from\nStarts today, owner is the person viewing\nEdit log entry 'Copied from ...'"
process p1 "The copy opens on the canvas, selected in the bar"
click c2 "Click 'Archive'"
overlay o1 "'Archive this workflow?'\n'An archived workflow is retired: new cases no longer use it. Cases already in progress keep it. It stays in the version history and can be duplicated into a new draft.'\n'Reason (optional)', 'Cancel', 'Archive'"
click c3 "Click 'Archive'"
store st2 "Status becomes Archived, a version line is kept with the reason"
toast t1 "'Summit Initial Authorization is archived'\n'It no longer matches new cases. Cases that follow it keep their version.'"
screen ar "The workflow stays in the list with an Archived pill\nNotice 'This workflow is archived, so it is read only. Duplicate it to start a new draft.'\n'Save draft' and 'Publish' are dimmed, 'Archive' is dimmed in the menu,\nevery setting and tool that changes something is dimmed"
decision d2 "Was it the only published workflow for its payer?"
process p2 "New cases for that payer use the labelled default process\nuntil another workflow is published"
click c4 "Click 'Cancel', X or Escape"
endx e2 "Nothing archived"
end e1 "A copy is ready to edit, or the workflow is retired"

s1 --> mn
mn --> c1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| o0 --> st1
d1 -->|No| st1
st1 --> p1 --> e1
mn --> c2 --> o1 --> c3 --> st2 --> t1 --> ar --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| p2 --> e1
d2 -->|No| e1
o1 --> c4 --> e2
